ntdll: the ARM64EC code map without a memory commitment on Haiku

Every ARM64EC process (an x86-64 program run through FEX) maps a bitmap with one bit per page of the address
space, 4 GiB for Wine's 47-bit user space, readable everywhere and written only where code is registered.
Wine maps it as committed read-only memory, which costs nothing on Linux. Haiku commits memory for every
readable private mapping (vm.cpp, vm_map_cache) unless it is mapped with MAP_NORESERVE (libroot's mmap makes
that an overcommitting area): 4 GiB on a 4 GB Raspberry Pi 4 fails, and alloc_arm64ec_map() ends the process
("failed to allocate ARM64EC map"). On Haiku the map is now reserved, mapped readable with MAP_NORESERVE, and
its pages recorded as committed; commit_arm64ec_map() makes parts of it writable as before, and Haiku
allocates those pages when they are written.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c	2026-10-22 02:54:03.676962151 +0200
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c	2026-10-22 02:54:03.693363236 +0200
@@ -2467,7 +2467,21 @@
     SIZE_T size = ((ULONG_PTR)address_space_limit + page_size) >> (page_shift + 3);  /* one bit per page */
 
     size = ROUND_SIZE( 0, size, host_page_mask );
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+    /* Haiku commits memory for every readable private mapping, here 4 GiB for a 47-bit address space,
+     * unless it is mapped with MAP_NORESERVE. The map is only written where commit_arm64ec_map() makes
+     * it writable; elsewhere it reads as zeros. So reserve it, map it readable without a commitment,
+     * and record its pages as committed */
+    status = map_view( &arm64ec_view, NULL, size, MEM_TOP_DOWN, VPROT_READ, 0, 0, 0 );
+    if (!status && anon_mmap_fixed( arm64ec_view->base, size, PROT_READ, MAP_NORESERVE ) == MAP_FAILED)
+    {
+        delete_view( arm64ec_view );
+        status = STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
+    }
+    if (!status) set_page_vprot( arm64ec_view->base, size, VPROT_READ | VPROT_COMMITTED );
+#else
     status = map_view( &arm64ec_view, NULL, size, MEM_TOP_DOWN, VPROT_READ | VPROT_COMMITTED, 0, 0, 0 );
+#endif
     if (status)
     {
         ERR( "failed to allocate ARM64EC map: %08x\n", status );
